@attribute [CustomPage("Components/Layout/Overview")]

<h1>Layout</h1>

<h2><code>Card</code></h2>
<p>A bordered, rounded surface that holds whatever it is given in <code>ChildContent</code>.</p>
<ul>
    <li><code>Title</code>: a bold heading at the top. Null shows a plain card with no heading and no aside.</li>
    <li><code>Aside</code>: muted text at the right of the title, e.g. "1 this week". It stays on one line. Only shown with a title.</li>
    <li><code>data-testid</code>: <code>TestId</code>, and <code>{TestId}-aside</code> on the aside.</li>
</ul>

<p>Stories: <a href="./?path=/docs/components-layout-card--docs">Card</a></p>

<h2><code>BottomNav</code></h2>
<p>The bar at the foot of a screen: the tabs in <code>Items</code> with a raised button between them. The tab equal to <code>Current</code> has a pill behind its icon, bold text and <code>aria-current="page"</code>; tapping it raises nothing. With an odd number of tabs the extra one goes left of the raised button.</p>
<ul>
    <li><code>AddLabel</code> and <code>AddIcon</code>: the raised button, a primary rounded square (<code>--radius-md</code>) of <code>--add-button-size</code>, lifted by <code>--add-button-lift</code> so its label is level with the tab labels. It is an action and is never current.</li>
    <li><code>AddHasPopup</code>: optional <code>aria-haspopup</code> value, e.g. <code>dialog</code>.</li>
    <li><code>OnNavigate</code> is raised with the tapped tab; <code>OnAdd</code> by the raised button.</li>
    <li><code>data-testid</code>: <code>bottom-nav</code>, <code>add-button</code> and each item's <code>TestId</code>.</li>
</ul>

<p>Stories: <a href="./?path=/docs/components-layout-bottomnav--docs">BottomNav</a></p>

<h2><code>AppScreen</code></h2>
<p>The frame of a screen: a top bar with <code>Title</code>, <code>Subtitle</code>, <code>Actions</code> and a back arrow, an optional <code>Toolbar</code>, the scrolling <code>ChildContent</code>, and a footer with <code>Status</code>, <code>BottomBar</code> and the bottom navigation bar, in that order from the top.</p>
<ul>
    <li><code>OnBack</code> shows the back arrow (<code>data-testid</code> <code>BackTestId</code>, default <code>back</code>) and takes Android back. Unset, Android back leaves the app, except on a top-level screen other than the first of <code>NavItems</code>: it raises <code>OnNavigate</code> with that first item.</li>
    <li><code>NavItems</code> makes the screen top-level and shows a <code>BottomNav</code> with <code>Current</code> marked; <code>AddLabel</code>, <code>AddIcon</code>, <code>AddHasPopup</code>, <code>AddButtonAttributes</code>, <code>OnNavigate</code> and <code>OnAdd</code> go to the bar.</li>
    <li><code>Status</code> sits in a polite live region above the bar, and above the raised button when there is one. Without a bar it floats over the foot of the content.</li>
    <li>The content ends clear of the raised button and the status message, so screens add no bottom padding of their own.</li>
    <li><code>OnRefresh</code> adds pull-to-refresh to the content; a failure to set it up is logged (9701) and the screen works without it.</li>
    <li><code>data-testid</code>: <code>screen-title</code>, <code>screen-subtitle</code>, <code>bottom-bar</code> and <code>pull-refresh</code>.</li>
</ul>

<p>Stories: <a href="./?path=/docs/components-layout-appscreen--docs">AppScreen</a></p>

<h2><code>StartupGate</code></h2>
<p>Runs <code>Initialize</code> once before showing its content, with a <code>StartupView</code> meanwhile. A failure is logged (9002) and shown; with <code>Retryable</code> (the default) Try again runs <code>Initialize</code> again. The app passes its own wording: <code>Title</code>, <code>LoadingLabel</code> and <code>FailedMessage</code>.</p>

<h2><code>StartupView</code></h2>
<p>The start-up screen: a spinner, or <code>FailedMessage</code> with Try again when <code>OnRetry</code> is set. <code>data-testid</code>: <code>startup-top-bar</code>, <code>startup-loading</code>, <code>startup-error</code> and <code>startup-retry</code>.</p>

<h2><code>AppErrorBoundary</code></h2>
<p>Shows an <code>ErrorView</code> instead of its content when the content throws, and logs the error (9101). Restart raises <code>OnRestart</code>, then shows the content again.</p>

<h2><code>ErrorView</code></h2>
<p>"Something went wrong" with a Restart button that raises <code>OnRestart</code>. <code>data-testid</code>: <code>error-top-bar</code>, <code>error-message</code>, <code>error-bottom-bar</code> and <code>error-restart</code>.</p>

<p>Stories: <a href="./?path=/docs/components-layout-startupgate--docs">StartupGate</a>, <a href="./?path=/docs/components-layout-startupview--docs">StartupView</a>, <a href="./?path=/docs/components-layout-apperrorboundary--docs">AppErrorBoundary</a>, <a href="./?path=/docs/components-layout-errorview--docs">ErrorView</a></p>
